A||N||9||Fieroman25||Fiero Sweetness (everybody read this)||||3||
Z||000000||Fieroman25||08-22-2000||02:42 PM||||I was at a car show at a mall near my house.  It was primarily classics which i'm interested in just as much.  Then i saw a pair of Vipers, I was getting excited and as I turned the corner i had to rub my eyes, in disbelief.  It was a fiero.  But the paint was a faded off white color.  As I walked closer it changed colors about 4 times.  It was the sweetest paint job i have ever seen.  Getting closer I notice the front air dam is very close to the ground.  The body was a 86-88 GT had the ram air side scoops and 17 in chrome wheels, and the reason the nose was so low was an ADDITIONAL front fascia below the the already low nose piece.  I was thinking how careful this guy must have to drive when i happenned to look into the engine compartment, and immediately had to shield my eyes.  With out a doubt this guy had the most chrome i have ever seen in any engine compartment, and i have been to my fair share of shows.  After i picked my jaw up off the ground, I noticed something very peculiar taking up the location of the air cleaner housing area.  DEAR LORD it was a turbo, with intercooler pipes running into the already small trunk space and straight down to a air box of some sort.  Then as I'm looking at this box under the car I see all the suspension work he did, with the swaybars almost hitting the ground.  I was so blown away.  As I came back to earth, i hear some guys talking behind me.  This is what I heard, "So man, ever run it down the track?"  "Yeah, one night i was messing around to get a baseline time, not even redlining it, and I ran 11.9"<P>I had a permanent smile on my face for the rest of the day.<P>Hope everyone thought this was a cool story, sorry it was so long, i got carried away.||||reg||3
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-22-2000||02:55 PM||||11.9!?!  That's incredible.  Was it still a 60-degree V6 (2.8/3.1/3.4) or some other engine?  Automatic or standard trans?  ||||reg||14
