Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||08-23-2000||10:45 PM||||I'd be a bit skeptical of the 11.9, but as far as the dropping, extra nose piece, and paint effect, well, if it was done for areodynamic and handling reasons, good call! if not, well, it's his money. The paint job I'd like to see, I saw one like that a few years ago at the milwaukee car show, first glance was purple, then blue, and by the time I passed it it was about yellow/greenish. I have since heard that those colors scemes require huge ammounts of labor and paint and can easily reach upwords towards the $10k mark!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jonathan||08-23-2000||11:25 PM||||I priced this paint for my repaint not too long ago.  The brand I checked out was called Khameleon.  They have eight color shifting shades.  I wanted the magenta to electric blue.  The price....sitting down???  $450.00/qt.  I was looking at two to three quarts to repaint.  This was just for the color.  Not the activators, or any of the other necessary chemicals.  OUCH  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>||||reg||4
Z||000007||Seanh||08-24-2000||03:02 PM||||I saw that paint at the Las Vegas SEMA show. I also was astounded as the price too, but thats about right $450/qt. I have a 2.8 with turbo and also a 4 speed auto and I made that run in 12.8 sec. (on full boost). I am taking it back down to Kansas once I get the new NorthStar in to see if I cant shave a little more time off that. Ill keep ya posted.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fieroman25||08-24-2000||03:41 PM||||Just to clarify, the engine was dierectly out of a Buick Turbo Grand National.  3.8 , i think 90 degree.||||reg||10
Z||000009||BBBAD GT||08-24-2000||05:04 PM||||Seanh:<P>Did you ever get pics of your twin turbo setup?  I'm sure alot of guys would be interested in how it ended up in the Fiero bay, and also the hardware.  <P>BTW, that GN motor still would have to be modified to run a 11.9.  A bone stock GN would do low 14's high 13's maybe at 3400lb (calcuated 260 hp), if you just drop the weight to say 2700lb, then calculated you should be doing only mid to high 12's (you would need in the ballpark of 300-320 to get yourself in the 11's at 2700lb).   <p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 08-24-2000).]||||reg||1
